Found 2026-09-30 in a live check against kube-apiserver v1.36.1 (via Net::Async::Kubernetes card 55). A {Str} map field (metadata.labels, metadata.annotations, ConfigMap data, ...) whose Perl value is numeric is emitted as a JSON number; the API server rejects the object with 400 BadRequest. Arrays of Str are already quoted correctly. Present in 1.108 too (not a regression).

Repro:
  my $n = 5; IO::K8s->new->new_object('ConfigMap', metadata => { name => 'y', labels => { v => $n+0 } }, data => { a => $n*2 })->to_json
  => {"data":{"a":10},..."labels":{"v":5}}  -- must be "10" and "5".

Expected: every value of a map-of-Str field serializes as a JSON string, the way [Str] arrays and scalar Str fields do (TO_JSON, to_json, to_yaml).

2026-09-30 05:55 Analysis (2026-09-30, unattended run): NOT fixed -- stopped per brief, fix is a design change too large for the 1.109 release eve. No test or code left in the tree.

Repro confirmed on HEAD 2d1d84e2: ConfigMap labels {v=>5+0}, annotations {a=>5*3}, data {a=>5*2, b=>'10' used in numeric context} -> to_json {"data":{"a":10,"b":10},..."annotations":{"a":15},"labels":{"s":10,"v":5}}; to_yaml emits them bare (a: 10). A real string '10' in data already comes out quoted in to_yaml ('10') since k188, so once values are strings YAML needs nothing.

Why no contained fix: { Str => 1 } / is_hash_of_str is not a string map in this codebase, it is THE opaque map ('map of string keys to anything'). Documented as such in Resource.pm (%HASH_VALUE_TYPES comment), CRD.pm _type_schema (emits opaque x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields), AutoGen (_scalar_kind, generic object and additionalProperties:{type:string} both -> { Str => 1 }, reuse matcher lines ~1013/1060/1080/1093), and pinned by a GUARD in t/108_k145_str_wire_type.t: spec => {replicas => 3} on a { Str => 1 } field must stay 3. Stringifying scalar values of every is_hash_of_str field would break that claim and real opaque fields: IO::K8s::APIObject default spec/status, WatchEvent.object, OpaqueDeviceConfiguration.parameters (RawExtension), Cilium CiliumNodeConfigSpec.defaults / CiliumExternalWorkload spec, Traefik MiddlewareSpec.plugin and ErrorPage.statusRewrites, ExternalSecrets OnePasswordProvider.vaults (map[string]int upstream), AgentSandbox podTemplate etc., and every AutoGen/CRD-generated opaque object field.

What a real fix needs (per-field classification, the registry cannot tell today):
1. A new DSL form + registry flag for a true map[string]string (name is an API decision: e.g. a typed-map entry in %HASH_VALUE_TYPES under a spelling other than Str, or an option on { Str => 1 }). TO_JSON branch mirrors is_array_of_str (defined && !ref ? "$v" : $v, new hash).
2. Reclassify every { Str => 1 } declaration whose upstream schema is additionalProperties:{type:string}: 210 declarations in 151 files (49 in 45 core Api/Apimachinery files: labels, annotations, data, stringData, binaryData, nodeSelector, matchLabels, selector, StorageClass/VolumeAttributesClass parameters, volumeAttributes, deprecatedTopology, allocatedResourceStatuses, attachmentMetadata, Flex options, ...). ResourceList fields (overhead, podFixed, allocatedResources, capacity) are really { Quantity => 1 }.
3. CRD.pm _type_schema (additionalProperties type string), CRD/Emitter.pm reverse mapping, compare_to_schema name, SpecBuilder flag list (line ~320).
4. AutoGen: additionalProperties {type:string} -> new form, plus the core-reuse matcher and a regenerated lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen/CoreShapes.pm (maint/core-shape-index-gen.pl, t/85) since ObjectMeta labels/annotations change shape.
5. Tests: the card's repro (labels, annotations, ConfigMap data, arithmetic values, numeric-context string, to_yaml '10' quoted) + guard that { Str => 1 } opaque stays untouched and typed maps ({Int},{Num},{Bool},{IntOrStr}) keep their types.
Suggest scheduling after 1.109; not a regression (present in 1.108). Interim workaround for callers: pass label/annotation/data values as strings ("$n").

